@startsalt
' Screen: Run Diff View
' Related user stories:
'   US-60: As a QA engineer, I want to compare two runs side-by-side to see regressions
'   US-61: As a QA engineer, I want to see per-turn score deltas between two runs
'   US-62: As a QA engineer, I want a verdict comparison banner at the top of the diff

{
  ' Header
  <b>Run Diff</b>  <i>Compare two runs step-by-step</i>
  ==
  ' Verdict comparison banner
  {+
    Run A: <b>R-2846</b>  checkout-flow v3 · gpt-4o v2   | Verdict: <color:green><b>PASS</b></color>  Score: <b>0.91</b>
    " "
    Run B: <b>R-2845</b>  checkout-flow v3 · gpt-4-turbo | Verdict: <color:red><b>FAIL</b></color>  Score: <b>0.41</b>
    --
    Overall Score Delta: <color:red><b>Δ -0.50</b></color>  ·  Verdict Regression: <color:green>PASS</color> → <color:red>FAIL</color>
  }
  ==
  ' Column headers
  {
    <b>Turn / Expectation</b>      | <b>Run A — gpt-4o v2</b>                         | <b>Run B — gpt-4-turbo v1</b>
    ==
    ' Step 1: User authored node (same in both)
    <b>Turn 1 · USER (authored)</b>
    | "I want to return my order #45892."            | "I want to return my order #45892."
    --
    ' Step 2: Agent response diff
    <b>Turn 2 · AGENT</b>          | Score: <color:green>0.92</color>                    | Score: <color:red>0.54</color>  Δ <color:red>-0.38</color>
    | "I'd be happy to help with your return"       | "Please provide your order number"
    | "for order #45892. I'm sorry it arrived"      | <color:red>"and reason for return."</color>
    | "damaged. Let me get this sorted."             | " "
    --
    ' Per-expectation breakdown: step 2
    <i>greeting</i>                | <color:green>✓ 1.00</color>                          | <color:green>✓ 1.00</color>  Δ 0.00
    <i>empathy</i>                 | <color:green>✓ 0.95</color>                          | <color:red>✗ 0.12</color>  Δ <color:red>-0.83</color>
    <i>order_lookup_called</i>     | <color:green>✓ 1.00</color>                          | <color:red>✗ 0.00</color>  Δ <color:red>-1.00</color>
    ==
    ' Step 3: Freeball user node
    <b>Turn 3 · USER (freeball)</b>
    | <color:darkorange>"What's the refund policy?"</color>               | <color:darkorange>"What's the refund policy?"</color>
    --
    ' Step 4: Agent response diff
    <b>Turn 4 · AGENT</b>          | Score: <color:green>0.92</color>                    | Score: <color:orange>0.78</color>  Δ <color:orange>-0.14</color>
    | "Our refund policy allows returns"            | "You can return items within 30 days."
    | "within 30 days. Damaged items get a"        | <color:red>"Contact support for damaged items."</color>
    | "full refund or replacement."                 | " "
    --
    <i>policy_accuracy</i>         | <color:green>✓ 0.92</color>                          | <color:orange>△ 0.78</color>  Δ <color:orange>-0.14</color>
    <i>damaged_item_path</i>        | <color:green>✓ 1.00</color>                          | <color:red>✗ 0.20</color>  Δ <color:red>-0.80</color>
  }
  ==
  {
    [ Export Diff JSON ] | [ Open Run A ] | [ Open Run B ] | [ ← Back to Runs ]
  }
}
@endsalt
